/collapse-to-invariant for Engineering Workflows and Code Reviews
Purpose
Use /collapse-to-invariant when a discussion has accumulated assumptions, urgency, blame, or speculative explanations faster than the team has accumulated evidence. In engineering, the method is not a replacement for debugging, incident management, architecture review, or security review. It is a short reasoning hygiene step that returns the conversation to observable behavior, explicit trade-offs, and reversible next actions.

Engineering boundary: We use this process to separate observations from hypotheses. It does not certify a root cause, assign intent, or justify an irreversible change without evidence.

The target invariant is the same as in the broader method, translated for engineering work:

Grounded engineering agency: the team can state what the system demonstrably does, what remains uncertain, which quality attribute matters, and the next smallest safe experiment.

Use it when…
Do not use it as…
